{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1776889237,"nonce":"96+nK0OJ/E7EOiV/Tn2BYfH5R6Y=","title":"Watcher auto-start: remove buggy in-memory started-issues set","message":"## Problem\nThe watcher's auto-start feature tracks already-started issues via an in-memory set + session dir check (CLAUDE.md). The in-memory set can become stale and prevent re-starting issues after:\n- Session rejection (session dir cleaned but in-memory set not cleared)\n- Watcher SIGHUP (reloads config but not the in-memory set)\n\n## Proposed Solution\nRemove the in-memory `_started_issues` set entirely. Rely solely on session dir existence check, which is authoritative and survives restarts.\n\n## Files\n- host/watcher/host_watcher.py (remove _started_issues set)\n\n## Tests\n- tests/watcher/test_host_watcher.py::test_auto_start_after_reject\n- tests/watcher/test_host_watcher.py::test_auto_start_after_sighup\n\nREQ: REQ-003 (session lifecycle)","files":null}]}